%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a1 Situated Activities
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Situated Activities record what stakeholders do today, under the conditions they actually work and live in. Our main concept is **Meaningful Connections** (social introductions between care home residents). The morning care routine is unrelated to the concept of social introductions and is documented separately below.

= In brief =

* A newcomer arrives among strangers, disoriented and with little say in the move (SA-01).
* Long-term residents often stay in their rooms for months, lacking a reason to come out (SA-02).
* Shyness, forgotten names, and uncertainty about what to say stall most first encounters (SA-03).
* Residents rarely invite a peer to spend time together, held back by fear of refusal or of intruding (SA-04).
* Staff introduce residents when their shift allows, but only know fragments of the residents' shared pasts.

